/-!
# The finite type quasi-coherent subalgebras of an algebra sheaf

Let `X` be a scheme and let `A` be a sheaf of commutative `𝒪_X`-algebras.  Stacks Tag 05JT says
two things about the finite type quasi-coherent subalgebras of `A`: that they form a directed
system, and that on a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme their canonical cocone is
colimiting.  This file sets up the vocabulary both assertions are stated in and proves the part
of directedness that does not depend on constructing joins.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.IsFiniteType`: an algebra sheaf is of finite type when its
  structural ring map is of finite type on every affine open.
* `FiniteTypeSubalgebra A`: the full subcategory of `CategoryTheory.Subobject A` on the
  subobjects that are quasi-coherent and of finite type.
* `finiteTypeSubalgebraDiagram A` and `finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone A`: that category viewed as a
  diagram of algebra sheaves, and its canonical cocone with vertex `A`.

## Main results

* `isFilteredOrEmpty_of_exists_join` and `isFiltered_of_exists_join`: `FiniteTypeSubalgebra A`
  is filtered as soon as it is nonempty and any two of its objects have a common upper bound in
  `Subobject A`.  This discharges the two parts of `CategoryTheory.IsFilteredOrEmpty` that are
  formal, leaving exactly the existence of joins.
* `isFiniteType_of_iso`: finite type is invariant under isomorphism of algebra sheaves, which is
  what lets the property be read off any representative of a subobject.
* `hasBinaryCoproducts`: two algebra sheaves on a scheme have a coproduct, namely their tensor
  product over the structure sheaf.
* `finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone_ι_app`: the component of the canonical cocone at a subobject is
  that subobject's inclusion into `A`.

## Implementation notes

`CategoryTheory.Subobject A` carries `CategoryTheory.Preorder.smallCategory`, so its morphisms
are a `Subsingleton` and `CategoryTheory.IsFilteredOrEmpty.cocone_maps` holds with the identity;
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.hom_ext` is needed to push that through the full subcategory,
whose morphisms are the one-field `CategoryTheory.InducedCategory.Hom` structure rather than
plain morphisms of `Subobject A`.  The remaining field, `cocone_objs`, is the whole content.

`isFiniteType_of_iso` goes through `RingHom.FiniteType.comp_surjective` rather than
`RingHom.FiniteType.comp`: the comparison map is an isomorphism of commutative rings, and
surjectivity of it is cheaper to produce than finite typeness.  The two structure maps are
related by `CategoryTheory.Under.w`, which states the triangle pre-trimmed.

## What is not done

Neither assertion of Tag 05JT is proved here, and the reason is the same for both: there is no
way at this Mathlib pin to *form* the subalgebra sheaf generated by two subalgebra sheaves.
Concretely, `CategoryTheory.Limits.HasImages (CategoryTheory.Under X.sheaf)` does not hold --
`Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Limits/Shapes/Images.lean` supplies `HasImages` only through
`CategoryTheory.Limits.HasStrongEpiMonoFactorisations`, whose instances at this pin are
`Type`, functor categories into `Type`, abelian categories and two order categories, none of
which covers sheaves of commutative rings.  Consequently:

* `CategoryTheory.Subobject.semilatticeSup`, which needs `HasImages` together with
  `CategoryTheory.Limits.HasBinaryCoproducts`, is unavailable, so `Subobject A` has no join.
  `HasImages` is the only one of the two that is missing: the coproducts are supplied by
  `hasBinaryCoproducts` below.  The meet is available too, since
  `CategoryTheory.Limits.HasPullbacks (CategoryTheory.Under X.sheaf)` holds and hence so does
  `CategoryTheory.Subobject.semilatticeInf`.  Meets are the wrong direction for a filtered
  category.
* `CategoryTheory.Subobject.orderBot` is also unavailable, since it needs
  `CategoryTheory.Limits.InitialMonoClass (CategoryTheory.Under X.sheaf)`, i.e. that every
  algebra sheaf has injective structure map, which is false.  So the nonemptiness of
  `FiniteTypeSubalgebra A` is not formal either: the object that witnesses it is the image of
  `𝒪_X` in `A`, and that is again an image.

Beyond forming the join, two further statements would be needed and are proved nowhere in the
tree: that the subalgebra sheaf generated by two quasi-coherent subalgebra sheaves is
quasi-coherent, and that its sections over an affine open are the subalgebra generated by the
sections.  Only the second is reduced to commutative algebra here, by
`Stacks.RingTheory.FiniteTypeSubalgebra.finiteType_of_sup_range_eq_top`.

The quasi-coherence half has an independent gap of its own: there is no transport of
`Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent` along an isomorphism of algebra sheaves, the
counterpart of `isFiniteType_of_iso` proved here.  Supplying it means producing an isomorphism of
the underlying modules, and `Mathlib/Algebra/Category/ModuleCat/Sheaf/ChangeOfRings.lean` has no
naturality of `SheafOfModules.restrictScalars` in the ring morphism to build it from.  Any route
to either assertion of Tag 05JT needs that transport, because a construction produces a concrete
monomorphism and the properties then have to be moved to the representative that
`CategoryTheory.Subobject.mk` chooses.

## References

* [The Stacks Project, Tag 05JT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05JT)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- An algebra sheaf is of finite type when its structural ring map is of finite type on every
affine open. -/
def IsFiniteType (A : AlgebraSheaf X) : Prop :=
  ∀ U : X.Opens, IsAffineOpen U → RingHom.FiniteType (A.hom.hom.app (.op U)).hom

end Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebras

open Stacks.RelativeSpec

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- The coproduct of two algebra sheaves on a scheme exists: it is their tensor product over the
structure sheaf, i.e. the pushout of their two structure morphisms. -/
instance hasBinaryCoproducts (X : Scheme.{u}) : HasBinaryCoproducts (AlgebraSheaf X) :=
  Stacks.UnderCoproducts.hasBinaryCoproducts

/-- Finite type of an algebra sheaf only depends on its isomorphism class: the two structural
ring maps over an affine open differ by composition with an isomorphism of commutative rings. -/
theorem isFiniteType_of_iso {A B : AlgebraSheaf X} (e : A ≅ B) (hA : A.IsFiniteType) :
    B.IsFiniteType := by
  intro U hU
  have hw : A.hom ≫ e.hom.right = B.hom := Under.w e.hom
  have happ : (B.hom.hom.app (.op U)).hom =
      (e.hom.right.hom.app (.op U)).hom.comp (A.hom.hom.app (.op U)).hom := by
    rw [← hw]; rfl
  have hinv : e.inv.right.hom.app (.op U) ≫ e.hom.right.hom.app (.op U) = 𝟙 _ :=
    congrArg (fun f : B ⟶ B => f.right.hom.app (.op U)) e.inv_hom_id
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (e.hom.right.hom.app (.op U)).hom := fun y =>
    ⟨(e.inv.right.hom.app (.op U)).hom y, congr($(hinv).hom y)⟩
  rw [happ]
  exact (hA U hU).comp_surjective hsurj

/-- **The category of finite type quasi-coherent subalgebras of an algebra sheaf.**  This is the
full subcategory of `CategoryTheory.Subobject A` on the subobjects whose underlying algebra
sheaf is quasi-coherent and of finite type. -/
abbrev FiniteTypeSubalgebra (A : AlgebraSheaf X) :=
  ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory fun B : Subobject A =>
    (B : AlgebraSheaf X).IsQuasicoherent ∧ (B : AlgebraSheaf X).IsFiniteType

/-- The diagram consisting of all finite type quasi-coherent subalgebras of `A`. -/
def finiteTypeSubalgebraDiagram (A : AlgebraSheaf X) :
    FiniteTypeSubalgebra A ⥤ AlgebraSheaf X :=
  ObjectProperty.ι _ ⋙ Subobject.underlying

/-- The canonical cocone of all finite type quasi-coherent subalgebras of `A`, with vertex `A`
and with the inclusions of the subobjects as its components. -/
def finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone (A : AlgebraSheaf X) : Cocone (finiteTypeSubalgebraDiagram A) :=
  Cocone.mk A
    { app := fun B => B.obj.arrow
      naturality := fun _ _ f => Subobject.underlying_arrow f.hom }

/-- The diagram of finite type quasi-coherent subalgebras of `A` sends a subalgebra to its
underlying algebra sheaf. -/
@[simp]
theorem finiteTypeSubalgebraDiagram_obj (A : AlgebraSheaf X) (B : FiniteTypeSubalgebra A) :
    (finiteTypeSubalgebraDiagram A).obj B = (B.obj : AlgebraSheaf X) :=
  rfl

/-- The vertex of the cocone of finite type quasi-coherent subalgebras of `A` is `A` itself. -/
@[simp]
theorem finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone_pt (A : AlgebraSheaf X) :
    (finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone A).pt = A :=
  rfl

/-- The component of the cocone of finite type quasi-coherent subalgebras of `A` at a subalgebra
is its inclusion into `A`. -/
@[simp]
theorem finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone_ι_app (A : AlgebraSheaf X) (B : FiniteTypeSubalgebra A) :
    (finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone A).ι.app B = B.obj.arrow :=
  rfl

/-- **The formal half of the directedness assertion of Stacks Tag 05JT.**  The finite type
quasi-coherent subalgebras of `A` form a filtered-or-empty category as soon as any two of them
are contained in a third.

The two remaining conditions are free: `CategoryTheory.Subobject A` is a preorder category, so
any two parallel morphisms between finite type quasi-coherent subalgebras agree and the identity
coequalizes them. -/
theorem isFilteredOrEmpty_of_exists_join (A : AlgebraSheaf X)
    (h : ∀ B C : FiniteTypeSubalgebra A, ∃ D : FiniteTypeSubalgebra A,
      B.obj ≤ D.obj ∧ C.obj ≤ D.obj) :
    IsFilteredOrEmpty (FiniteTypeSubalgebra A) where
  cocone_objs B C :=
    ⟨(h B C).choose, ObjectProperty.homMk (h B C).choose_spec.1.hom,
      ObjectProperty.homMk (h B C).choose_spec.2.hom, trivial⟩
  cocone_maps _ Y f g :=
    ⟨Y, 𝟙 Y, by rw [ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ (Subsingleton.elim f.hom g.hom)]⟩

/-- **The formal half of the directedness assertion of Stacks Tag 05JT.**  The finite type
quasi-coherent subalgebras of `A` form a filtered category as soon as there is one of them and
any two of them are contained in a third. -/
theorem isFiltered_of_exists_join (A : AlgebraSheaf X)
    (hne : Nonempty (FiniteTypeSubalgebra A))
    (h : ∀ B C : FiniteTypeSubalgebra A, ∃ D : FiniteTypeSubalgebra A,
      B.obj ≤ D.obj ∧ C.obj ≤ D.obj) :
    IsFiltered (FiniteTypeSubalgebra A) :=
  let := hne
  let := isFilteredOrEmpty_of_exists_join A h
  IsFiltered.mk

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebras
